        "original_id": "1bbcd9ff-8994-587e-9fd3-4d8b0665439a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Richard Wagner, Jules Massenet, Henri Meilhac, Philippe Gille, Abbé Prévost, Emil Scaria\n- Works: Parsifal, Manon, L’histoire du chevalier des Grieux et de Manon Lescaut\n- Places: Bayreuth\n- Roles: Gurnemanz\n\nFacts:\n- In 1731, Abbé Prévost wrote the novel L’histoire du chevalier des Grieux et de Manon Lescaut.\n- In 1882, Emil Scaria created the role of Gurnemanz in Parsifal for Richard Wagner at Bayreuth.\n- Parsifal, cataloged as WWV 111, is an opera in three acts by German composer Richard Wagner.\n- Manon is an opéra comique in five acts by Jules Massenet.\n- Manon uses a French libretto by Henri Meilhac and Philippe Gille.\n- Manon is based on Abbé Prévost’s 1731 novel L’histoire du chevalier des Grieux et de Manon Lescaut.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
